==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{bor|en|LL.|spīnālis||of or belonging to the spine}}, from {{af|la|spīna|-ālis|t1=a prickle, spine|t2=-al|pos2=adjectival suffix|nocat=1}}; {{l|en|surface analysis#Noun}}, {{suffix|en|spine|-al}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/spaɪ.nəl/|/spaɪ.nl̩/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-spinal.wav|Audio (Southern England)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪnəl|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|-}}

# {{lb|en|anatomy|zootomy}} Of or relating to the [[spine]].
## Of or pertaining to the [[spinal cord]].
## {{lb|en|zoology}} {{q|of a [[frog]] or other [[experimental]] animal}} Having a [[pithed]] [[brain]], but an [[intact]] [[surgically]] [[isolate]]d [[spinal cord]].

